{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"94ebfbf8fe12772a","type":"text","text":"**Prepared Enchantments.** Prepared enchantments roll one **Spellcraft** die higher. Prepared enchantments have a **Spellcraft Roll** charges and regain a **Spellcraft Roll** charges to a max of your **Spellcraft [[Die Max]]** \nCreatures can attempt to use the item past that, but it uses their stats (usually **Spellcraft**) as appropriate.","x":-140,"y":-420,"width":440,"height":200},
		{"id":"b6b45caeddd8762e","type":"text","text":"**Complex Enchantments.** Casters can create more complex enchantments (Something that would take multiple spells). These enchantments cost more than one enchantment slot, but can not exceed half the max **Spellcraft** die. Additionally, the caster has enchantment slots equal to their **Spellcraft [[Die Max]]**","x":-140,"y":-700,"width":440,"height":180},
		{"id":"d4dc155d8db2b0bd","type":"text","text":"**Incomprehensible Enchantments.** Casters can make most any enchantment, now able to spend as many enchantment slots as the can access for it. Additionally, these slots are now double their **Spellcraft [[Die Max]]**","x":-140,"y":-960,"width":440,"height":160},
		{"id":"7e47a6a84b8f97de","type":"text","text":"**Explosive Disenchantment.** Caster can remove one enchantment of theirs within line of sight to cause an explosion. This explosion goes out for 5' per enchantment slot, dealing **[Minor Phyisical Harm](Harm)** per enchantment slot","x":-140,"y":-1700,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"#000000"},
		{"id":"5148f3411906a9c6","type":"text","text":"**Harness.** Caster can remove one enchantment of theirs within line of sight to add a die to a roll","x":360,"y":-910,"width":440,"height":60},
		{"id":"3cdb4598618de244","type":"text","text":"**Transfer Enchantment.** Caster can remove one enchantment of theirs within line of sight and place it on a non-magical item. The original item acts as described for removing enchantments. If the enchantment is removed from the non-magical item, the item will return to being non-magical (and does not behave as described for removing enchantments)","x":-660,"y":-1000,"width":440,"height":240},
		{"id":"e23600a5869383a1","type":"text","text":"**Enchantment Thief.** Caster can affect other enchantments as if their own. If they are a different magic or higher level, they must make a **Spellcraft** check to do so","x":-720,"y":-1222,"width":440,"height":125},
		{"id":"30559a700f23c848","type":"text","text":"**Orchestrator.** Caster can affect their enchantmented items at once using **Spellcraft**","x":360,"y":-1203,"width":440,"height":87},
		{"id":"a544e4f4386e6e16","type":"text","text":"**Master Enchanter.** Add double the points invested in **Spellcraft** and **Enchantment** when determining max enchantment slots","x":-140,"y":-1209,"width":440,"height":100},
		{"id":"e3773d8bafc9d9fb","type":"text","text":"**Enchantment.** Spells cast on items, cast using the caster's ability. Can be done in free time for potent long-term effect or quick for weak temp. effect\n==You can make temporary magic items. These items have 1 charge and have **Spellcraft** dice equal to the number of skills obtained in this branch. You may make an amount of Enchantments equal to half your **Spellcraft** die. If you would exceed this, you may choose to remove the magic from an enchantment you have made. You, or another creature may utilize it by rolling spellcraft==","x":-140,"y":-120,"width":440,"height":312}
	],
